            "The practical consequence: adopting Scrum alone does not give a team the ability to release working software every Sprint. If the Increment cannot meet the [Definition of Done](" + A + "definition-of-done/) without a manual test phase, the bottleneck is technical, and the fix is in the engineering practices rather than in the Scrum events.",
            "Read our comparison of [Agile methodologies](" + A + "types-of-agile-methodologies/) for Lean, Crystal, DSDM and FDD, and [Kanban vs Scrum](" + K + "kanban-vs-scrum/) for choosing between the two main frameworks.",
